      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc65Ycud",
      "path": "lib/src/compaction/structured/engine.dart",
      "line": 175,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —\n⚠️ **IMPORTANT: AC1 \"one basis\" invariant has a reachable counterexample — boundary-less windowed resumes re-arm phantom anchors through `refreshAgentState`**\n\nThe fix makes the projection the single anchor authority, and `_resetStaleUsageAnchors` (session_tree.dart:874-886) resets only entries **before the last boundary record** (`CompactionRecord` / `HiddenRangeRecord` / `CompactCheckpointRecord`). A resident tail that contains **no** boundary record returns `staleEntryIds = const {}`, so the rebuild at this line re-arms every persisted generation-time usage anchor — exactly the anchors the CLI's resume path deliberately zeroed one line after loading:\n\n- `lib/src/cli/session_commands.dart:962` — `_agent.state.messages = resetLoadedUsageAnchors(messages)` with the comment: *\"Loaded usage anchors are generation-time: post-compaction they phantom-report the pre-compaction size (183k on a 27k branch) and fire a no-op compaction on every resume. Re-anchor at chars/4.\"*\n\n**The divergent sequence**: a windowed resume whose boundary-walk exhausts `maxPages` (session_commands.dart logs *\"boundary-walk exhausted maxPages; proceeding with the tail window\"*) leaves a boundary-less giant tail; the resume zeroes anchors → the gate arms on the chars/4 basis; the engine's refresh at this line then re-arms the persisted phantom anchor → `estimateRequestTokens` anchors at the pre-trim size (`token_estimation.dart:489-493` — any anchor suppresses the overhead addend and prices the whole request). Engine basis ≠ gate basis — the gh-2237 divergence class, opposite direction: the engine chases the phantom number, folds/hides far past the real over-amount, and burns hide/checkpoint provider passes until a fold's own `HiddenRangeRecord` lands a boundary and re-collapses the basis. Cost is bounded (one over-aggressive fold, self-healing, hides are expandable) — that is why this is ⚠️, not 🚨 — but the PR's headline claim (\"the engine cannot re-derive a different basis than the gate that armed it\", PR description AC1) is falsified on this path, and no test pins it: UT-2 requires a boundary, E2 requires no anchors at all; the boundary-less windowed-resume case is exactly the gap between them.\n\n**Ask**: either extend the stale-anchor curation to cover load-time anchors whose generation context the resident tail cannot vouch for (the `resetLoadedUsageAnchors` rationale, applied at projection level for boundary-less tails), or state in `refreshAgentState`'s contract why the boundary-less resume basis is acceptable and pin the decision with a UT (gate basis vs engine basis after a `maxPages`-exhausted resume, no boundary records). Pre-fix, the blanket zero made this specific path correct (engine basis = gate basis = chars/4); please confirm the regression is intended or covered elsewhere before merge."
    }
  ],
  "census": {
    "source": "graphql",
    "graphqlTotal": 1,
    "graphqlUnresolved": 1
  }
